For more information, visit wppmedia.com .

Ongoing intake, but limited spots available&nbsp;
&nbsp;&nbsp;
As an intern within Paid Search, you will join a dedicated team and work with digital marketing, focusing on paid advertising across search engines. With us, you will have the opportunity to work with some of Sweden's and the world's most ambitious brands using market-leading technology. We place great emphasis on developing our teams, and in close collaboration with platforms, you will be involved in testing new creative formats and solutions. &nbsp;

Our office is located on Birger Jarlsgatan in Stockholm, and for the right candidate, there may be opportunities to continue your career with us after the internship.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Who are you?&nbsp;
&nbsp;
We believe you’re a student in media, marketing or economics, and have a strong interest in digital marketing. You’re eager to learn, contribute with new ideas, have a self-driven attitude, detail-oriented, and enjoy working closely with others.

To join our team as an intern, you need to:

• Be available for at least 8 weeks

• Do your internship through a school or the Swedish Public Employment Service (Arbetsförmedlingen)

• Be available full-time during standard office hours

• Be fluent in Swedish and comfortable using English

• Be available to work full-time at our office in Stockholm with some hybrid flexibility

Please note: this internship is unpaid.&nbsp;

Interested?&nbsp;
Apply with your CV and include a short note about why you’d like to intern with us. Be sure to include the period you're applying for.&nbsp;
&nbsp;&nbsp;
Contact&nbsp;
If you have questions about the Paid Search internship, contact Hanna Cleve, Senior Activation Manager at hanna.cleve@wppmedia.com . Due to GDPR, we do not accept applications via email. &nbsp;

Please read our Privacy Notice &nbsp; for more information on how we process the information you provide. &nbsp;

Category: IT Services

Location:

For an international organization in New York, we are urgently looking for a REMOTE Data Lakehouse/BI Specialist. Candidates should be an experienced hands-on data lakehouse specialist with a history of working in an agile environment. Ideally, candidates should have hands on experience in designing and implementing data lakehouse architecture.

Candidates need to be fluent in English. All positions are long-term. This position is open for contractors and employees.

Candidates need to be able to work 4-6 hours per day in the normal office hours of New York, US.

Tasks and responsibilities:

​

• Work with an agile team to design and implement data lakehouse architecture and BI models;

• Translate design specifications and functional requirements into data lakehouse architecture and BI models;

• Data import, transformation and loading to data lakehouse from MongoDB;

• Develop and implement data visualization and interactive dashboards;

• Merge code into shared repositories, validate code, and perform quality assurance;

• Implement BI-based dashboard reporting to generate and share insights;

Profile:

• +2 years of experience working with AWS BI and data lakehouse tools;

• Experience designing and implementing data lakehouse;

• Experience designing and implementing BI data visualization and interactive dashboards;

• Experience with Kafka or other similar large-scale messaging technologies;

• Experience implementing BI-based dashboard reporting;

• Experience with MEAN stack framework is an advantage;

• Knowledge and understanding of SDLC and Agile/Scrum procedures, CI/CD and Automation;

Offered:

• A challenging role for an international organization in New York;

